# L0 full-message chronological lookup

This component implements the previously proposed oracle-log lookup as a lazy
instruction stream for the actual bounded lifetime. It changes no frozen game,
source backend, primitive assumption or production gate. The actual factory
sets N=T*(2^20+2), stored-key capacity215150 bytes and response2112 bits. T may
be zero; the zero-record circuit still performs two base calls. The caller
separately supplies a finite full-message capacity and byte-length bit width.
The actual factory requires capacity at least the retained6882996-byte honest
envelope; query count does not imply a message-length bound.

`OverlayLookup` lays out a persistent array followed by query, enable, response
and clean work. Each record is active1, length b, padded key8W, padded value v.
The query carries length b and its entire message capacity. Layout and resource
methods use constant-size dictionaries of integer intervals. Gate emission
does not allocate an N-slot array, materialize a key-wide control tuple or use
a data-dependent wire address. Actual lifetime layouts can therefore be
described without executing an infeasibly large circuit.

For every slot the circuit computes enable AND active AND equality of the
length and first W bytes. It restores the temporarily modified key before any
base call. Reverse suffix flags identify the highest matching slot. It copies
only that stored value, or the base response on a miss, then clears every
match, suffix, ladder, hit and response-work bit. Lookup accepts holes and
duplicate keys; no canonical append-counter invariant is needed. Active keys
must still be canonical encodings with declared length at most W.

The full query is passed to the provided base interface, including the tail
beyond W. A legal query has length within its supplied capacity and canonical
zero padding. If its length exceeds W it cannot match an active stored key;
matching the compared length and head is otherwise full-address equality.
No additional promise bounds the contents or excludes repeated queries.

## One fixed provided function

The compact instruction is

```text
('F:variable', length_start, b, message_start, message_capacity_bytes,
 response_start, response_bits)
```

Its arguments describe disjoint wire intervals, including the complete
message. It calls a supplied response-XOR oracle on the canonical variable
length encoding. Every fixed `F:length` adapter is a restriction of this same
immutable F. There are no independent functions for distinct lengths or
capacities. The finite experiment supplies one fixed total extension on
noncanonical register encodings; this component interprets only legal query
encodings as source messages and does not give a free validation adapter.

For the actual source interface, F already has the domain-padded264-byte
response required by frozen C-1. The native widths at extended L256 are:

| Domain-last byte | Meaning | Native response bits |
|---|---|---:|
|0|Extended H0|1024|
|1|H1|512|
|3|H3|384|
|4|H4|128|
|5|H5 for the two frozen rows|10|
|8|mu|512|
|9|Challenge1|2112|
|10|Challenge2|832|
|11|Challenge3|256|

The source H5 squeezes two bytes but masks the result to ten bits here; its
second byte's high six bits are also zero. Source-domain response bits beyond
these widths are zero. This is a property of the provided typed oracle, not a
free operation converting an arbitrary raw-XOF response into the right one.
Unrecognized/empty source addresses retain one explicit experiment-supplied
fixed total completion. The earlier note does not define that completion;
this component neither invents fresh extra output nor certifies a broader
external-access experiment. Interface acceptance remains open.

Generic `OverlayLookup(...,value_bits=v)` instances permit smaller synthetic
v-bit oracle contracts for structural controls. These are not a free prefix
adapter to the actual264-byte base oracle: they allocate only v response-work
bits, whereas such an adapter must compute and clear the full2112 bits.
The source factory always uses2112.
General routing tests use arbitrary immutable responses, establishing a
stronger local clean-map property; source-interface tests additionally impose
the native padding and check equality with the fixed-length adapters.

Two base calls are unconditional, even on a match or when enable is zero.
The first computes F into clean work, the second clears it. F, full query and
the log must stay unchanged between those calls. A stateful/logging oracle is
not that contract; the negative control demonstrates residual work for one.

## Exact local resource and state statement

For N>0 and k=b+8W the emitted counts are:

```text
X =4kN+4N+2
CNOT =4kN
Toffoli =N*(4k+6+v)+v+2
base calls =2
clean work =2N+k+v+2 bits
```

For N=0 the circuit has v Toffolis, two base calls and v clean work bits.
One Toffoli is charged as five elementary two-qubit gates, as in the reviewed
prior construction. Persistent log, full query, enable and caller response
are separately inventoried; append counter belongs to W0 and is not included
again here. Base-oracle retained state and physical compilation are external.

The explicit phase-free gates establish the clean XOR map for each basis
state with legal canonical encodings and zero work. Linearity extends this
map to superpositions correlated with the retained log, F and an external
reference. The response may be arbitrary beforehand. This local identity
does not assert that tracing away retained input/log/reference registers
preserves their reduced state, or establish the full sampler/adversary
projection. Honest source requests remain classical and atomic.

Fifty focused tests passed on the current candidate. They exhaust three-slot
one-bit key/value histories including holes, duplicates, query/enable/target
choices; check long messages, empty messages and length separation; compare
emitted counts against the independent retained formula; compare same-F fixed
and variable interfaces and native padding; and detect missing uncompute,
stateful base behavior, malformed factories and source drift. Full actual
lifetime circuits are not executed. Five selected source/spec pins are checked
before and after the actual factory; this is not a dependency closure.

